{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChS4t1XBLbyLbCRU19o23","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic-assignment rule now skips values that are upper-case snake-case environment variable names. The log scan, the committer's scan and the diff guard share the rule, so all three change together.\n\n`go test ./internal/...` passes, including `internal/redact`, and `go vet` and `gofmt` are clean on that package. A full `go test ./...` hit my 2-minute tool timeout, so I did not get a clean full-repo run.\n\n- **The skip:** in `internal/redact/rules.go`, a value counts as an env name if it has at least one underscore, only upper-case letters and digits, and is at most 64 bytes. `placeholder()` calls this check, so it covers both quoted and unquoted values.\n- **New negatives:** the three acceptance inputs from the issue now produce no findings.\n- **Boundaries:** a new table test in `internal/redact/scan_test.go`, `TestScannerGenericAssignmentEnvNameBoundaries`, checks that values just outside the pattern are still reported. These are 65 characters, no underscore, mixed or lower case, a trailing dot, plus, slash or equals, a leading underscore or digit, and a double underscore. The existing true-positive tests are untouched.\n- **No doc change:** the proposal has no paragraph on this rule.\n\nI wrote the report to `.ard/388/worker-engineer.md`. I did not commit or push anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_read_input_tokens":23291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534},"output_tokens":456,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84e10a9b-3ea9-4404-b4b6-125deb9fee19","uuid":"35a8f462-d73c-4b7b-bd40-125